                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bluff",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87c87539-1c51-3ced-98aa-dce94c45af1b",
                                        "entry_id": "818e8618-e8a1-316b-8518-a824605a7286",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a bluff; to give the impression that one’s hand is stronger than it is."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f44f7bc4-f6c3-4ac8-8264-3833b9525b1f",
                                                "sense_id": "87c87539-1c51-3ced-98aa-dce94c45af1b",
                                                "text": "John bluffed by betting without even a pair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e09c3ce0-5ec3-3943-951a-f8ebe36ee663",
                                        "entry_id": "818e8618-e8a1-316b-8518-a824605a7286",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To frighten, deter, or deceive with a false show of strength or confidence; to give a false impression of strength or temerity in order to intimidate or gain some advantage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b517356-c569-4629-905c-b14138a3fbc1",
                                                "sense_id": "e09c3ce0-5ec3-3943-951a-f8ebe36ee663",
                                                "text": "The government claims it will call an election if this bill does not pass. Is it truly ready to do so, or is it bluffing?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08b38c96-2783-3825-80a3-fcbde9836b4f",
                                        "entry_id": "818e8618-e8a1-316b-8518-a824605a7286",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To perform or achieve by bluffing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81fad9b1-eac4-43ce-8a91-6008fdfa660d",
                                                "sense_id": "08b38c96-2783-3825-80a3-fcbde9836b4f",
                                                "text": "We bluffed our way past the guards."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df792de7-302e-3f2e-9259-82afe8a4a3b9",
                                        "entry_id": "818e8618-e8a1-316b-8518-a824605a7286",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give false information intentionally, to lie (to someone), to deceive; to put on an act."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Manglish",
                                            "Singlish"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c81ea19c-43b7-4e0e-8210-9a969c6261df",
                                                "sense_id": "df792de7-302e-3f2e-9259-82afe8a4a3b9",
                                                "text": "Vinod, you want to bluff the doctor, your mother, father, uncle, auntie, CMPB all that I don't care. But you cannot bluff me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bluff",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8288986d-f0f3-33e4-a260-3ce0600706dd",
                                        "entry_id": "972d896f-8647-38bd-9cad-eec80db3b507",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A high, steep bank, for example by a river or the sea, or beside a ravine or plain; a cliff with a broad face."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e4bc145-a4b9-4049-bd5b-8d7bad631eb8",
                                                "sense_id": "8288986d-f0f3-33e4-a260-3ce0600706dd",
                                                "text": "In the sketch (which is taken about 75 Jovian days after that of the 2nd July) there is shown a dark copper-coloured streak along the southern margin of the south brown belt, butting on to a bluff-headed streak of cumulus cloud which may be the same remarkable bluff head noticed on July 2."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "898b402c-cf78-4d70-931e-1c5b4225a45e",
                                                "sense_id": "8288986d-f0f3-33e4-a260-3ce0600706dd",
                                                "text": "It seems there was a worm that slept upon a pile of treasure, which it had zealously heaped up under a stone bluff."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1d2a793-2020-41d9-8fbb-ba3da6a18242",
                                                "sense_id": "8288986d-f0f3-33e4-a260-3ce0600706dd",
                                                "text": "Bounded to the north and west by mountains and river, to the east by river alone, and to the south by high bluffs that mark the beginning of the loess country, it is a compact and easily defended territory hospitable only to nomads. Today these lands are divided between the Inner Mongolian Autonomous Region and the Ning-hsia Hui Autonomous Region. Under the Republic the Ho-t’ao and Pao-t’ou plains were included in Sui-yuan province, and the Ning-hsia area in Ning-hsia province."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9011249e-a6ab-4541-8109-0cb2a64c73d4",
                                                "sense_id": "8288986d-f0f3-33e4-a260-3ce0600706dd",
                                                "text": "Situated on bluffs above the Huangpu, a tributary of the Yangtze, Shanghai—which means ‘above the sea’—is sinking."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e20476f-8310-34ee-9c1e-aed7a9fc0b60",
                                        "entry_id": "972d896f-8647-38bd-9cad-eec80db3b507",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small wood or stand of trees, typically poplar or willow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canadian-Prairies"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bluff",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2303a9d7-1ee5-34c3-9a64-5167ae281c5c",
